WEBVTT

00:00:00.580 --> 00:00:03.760
"The nation is fallen, yet mountains 
and rivers still exist.

00:00:03.760 --> 00:00:07.480
In spring, in the city, trees and grasses thrive."

00:00:08.070 --> 00:00:13.120
Did Hideyoshi's dream of a united 
nation die along with him?

00:00:13.540 --> 00:00:16.030
What does fate have in store?

00:00:16.030 --> 00:00:17.490
A peaceful world at last?

00:00:17.860 --> 00:00:19.840
Or even more warfare?

00:00:21.300 --> 00:00:23.460
Following the Battle of Sekigahara,

00:00:23.750 --> 00:00:26.460
the Uesugi clan, which had sided 
with the defeated Mitsunari,

00:00:26.460 --> 00:00:30.210
was handed a harsh punishment 
by the Tokugawa clan,

00:00:30.210 --> 00:00:32.210
including a change of domain 
and a reduced income.

00:00:33.080 --> 00:00:34.970
Their chief retainer, Kanetsugu,

00:00:35.310 --> 00:00:37.220
was initially prepared to go to war.

00:00:37.760 --> 00:00:39.970
But following Nobuyuki's impassioned pleas,

00:00:40.570 --> 00:00:42.470
he decided to accept the sentence,

00:00:42.470 --> 00:00:44.470
in order to protect the Uesugi clan.

00:00:45.630 --> 00:00:50.230
Meanwhile, Yukimura was exiled to Kudoyama and,

00:00:50.720 --> 00:00:52.900
having lost his purpose in life,

00:00:53.150 --> 00:00:54.820
was idling away his days.

00:00:56.360 --> 00:00:59.030
He even refused to accept a memento of Mitsunari

00:00:59.030 --> 00:01:01.080
that Nene had come to give him.

00:01:03.190 --> 00:01:07.170
But his meeting with Suzu, a girl from the village,

00:01:07.340 --> 00:01:11.130
gave Yukimura some peace of mind.

00:01:11.650 --> 00:01:14.000
And when she fell ill,

00:01:14.620 --> 00:01:18.530
he disobeyed his orders to stay 
confined to his home,

00:01:18.530 --> 00:01:21.930
and descended the mountain in 
order to take her to a doctor.

00:01:24.190 --> 00:01:24.930
As a result,

00:01:25.520 --> 00:01:30.950
Yukimura was placed under 
even stricter supervision.

00:03:01.910 --> 00:03:06.870
<i>Episode 7</i>

00:03:01.910 --> 00:03:06.870
<i>The Crimson Blade</i>

00:03:07.370 --> 00:03:13.380
Kudoyama

00:03:07.440 --> 00:03:13.630
Yukimura Sanada's days of exile at Kudoyama 
showed no signs of ending.

00:03:14.230 --> 00:03:16.640
For breaking the rules and 
descending the mountain,

00:03:16.640 --> 00:03:18.880
he was placed under stricter security,

00:03:19.230 --> 00:03:24.190
and no longer allowed to even set 
foot outside the premises.

00:03:29.760 --> 00:03:33.120
Hey, Miss, can't Lord Yukimura come outside?

00:03:33.120 --> 00:03:36.060
We've yet to thank him for saving her life.

00:03:37.580 --> 00:03:38.900
It's all our fault.

00:03:39.640 --> 00:03:41.710
Oh, don't worry about it.

00:03:42.860 --> 00:03:44.240
<i>Lord Yukimura...</i>

00:03:56.700 --> 00:03:58.650
Where are you going, Tsukimaru?

00:04:02.440 --> 00:04:03.840
Tsukimaru!

00:04:11.220 --> 00:04:12.380
Ina!

00:04:16.890 --> 00:04:19.510
While I'm glad the girl is all right,

00:04:19.510 --> 00:04:21.630
that was quite reckless of you both.

00:04:22.840 --> 00:04:26.380
Lord Yukimura doesn't regret his actions.

00:04:29.130 --> 00:04:33.620
But if he makes a scene again, 
things might get much worse.

00:04:34.300 --> 00:04:36.030
Wait, do you mean...

00:04:37.840 --> 00:04:40.690
He could be struck with a harsher punishment.

00:04:41.010 --> 00:04:42.160
Oh, no...

00:04:42.990 --> 00:04:47.000
When we achieve a lasting peace, 
I'm sure Yukimura will get pardoned.

00:04:47.470 --> 00:04:51.220
So I want him to hold out until that day comes.

00:04:55.180 --> 00:04:57.020
Please take care of him.

00:04:57.570 --> 00:04:59.330
You are my only hope!

00:05:01.980 --> 00:05:03.100
Ina...

00:05:06.600 --> 00:05:07.940
Oh, right.

00:05:07.940 --> 00:05:09.740
I brought some things for both of you!

00:05:11.190 --> 00:05:13.910
They'll help you deal with all 
the inconveniences here.

00:05:14.700 --> 00:05:16.920
Thank you so much!

00:05:17.180 --> 00:05:18.940
That's the Ina I know and love!

00:05:23.350 --> 00:05:26.200
Until next time, Ina!

00:05:31.040 --> 00:05:32.640
Now, then...

00:05:34.820 --> 00:05:37.690
How am I supposed to take all of this back?!

00:05:38.190 --> 00:05:44.150
Osaka Castle

00:05:38.830 --> 00:05:41.150
Meanwhile, Nobuyuki Sanada,

00:05:41.150 --> 00:05:43.270
as Ieyasu Tokugawa's messenger,

00:05:43.270 --> 00:05:47.200
made his way to Osaka Castle, 
to meet Hideyori Toyotomi.

00:05:47.830 --> 00:05:50.240
I'm here to report that the other day,

00:05:50.240 --> 00:05:52.700
after Lord Ieyasu Tokugawa 
gave up his post as shogun,

00:05:52.700 --> 00:05:57.580
the Imperial Court appointed his son, Lord Hidetada,

00:05:57.940 --> 00:06:00.800
as the second Tokugawa shogun.

00:06:02.250 --> 00:06:05.880
H-How could this be? What about Lord Hideyori?!

00:06:07.880 --> 00:06:09.320
How formal...

00:06:10.480 --> 00:06:12.860
Why don't you relax a little?

00:06:13.560 --> 00:06:15.390
I'm afraid I cannot.

00:06:15.990 --> 00:06:17.540
That's fine.

00:06:17.990 --> 00:06:19.930
Anyway, correct me if I'm wrong here.

00:06:21.140 --> 00:06:23.200
The appointment of the second Tokugawa shogun

00:06:23.710 --> 00:06:26.050
means that they refuse to return the country

00:06:26.550 --> 00:06:27.650
to the Toyotomi clan, yes?

00:06:32.500 --> 00:06:33.760
Anything else?

00:06:33.760 --> 00:06:34.730
Yes.

00:06:34.730 --> 00:06:37.880
Lord Ieyasu wishes to arrange a meeting with you

00:06:37.880 --> 00:06:41.320
to discuss future governance.

00:06:41.320 --> 00:06:42.560
A meeting?

00:06:44.290 --> 00:06:45.600
He insists.

00:06:50.120 --> 00:06:51.550
I won't go to Edo.

00:06:52.170 --> 00:06:53.590
You do not need to.

00:06:54.150 --> 00:06:58.560
As per the imperial proclamation, 
Lord Ieyasu will be heading to Kyoto.

00:06:59.210 --> 00:07:03.230
Therefore, he'd like to see you at Nijo Castle.

00:07:03.230 --> 00:07:07.080
He wishes to summon Lord Hideyori, 
as an aside to his trip to the capital?!

00:07:07.080 --> 00:07:08.490
Learn your place!

00:07:08.700 --> 00:07:09.770
Settle down.

00:07:10.100 --> 00:07:11.700
Lord Hideyori...

00:07:13.810 --> 00:07:17.490
I cannot give you an immediate reply.

00:07:18.020 --> 00:07:23.150
I cannot decide political matters 
such as these on my own.

00:07:24.770 --> 00:07:25.770
Kai,

00:07:25.770 --> 00:07:28.360
prepare a room for Lord Nobuyuki.

00:07:28.360 --> 00:07:29.290
Yes, sir.

00:07:33.740 --> 00:07:34.820
Oh, right.

00:07:35.560 --> 00:07:38.010
I wonder how Yukimura's doing.

00:07:47.340 --> 00:07:51.030
That stuff gets on my nerves, you know?

00:07:51.240 --> 00:07:52.870
What do you mean?

00:07:52.870 --> 00:07:56.730
I'm amazed Lord Tokugawa can 
devise such nasty things.

00:07:56.730 --> 00:07:59.490
Just listening to it annoys me.

00:08:02.800 --> 00:08:05.790
Is Lord Hideyori always like that?

00:08:06.750 --> 00:08:08.380
Like what?

00:08:08.380 --> 00:08:09.740
I'm not sure how to put it.

00:08:10.180 --> 00:08:12.550
You mean acting all high and mighty?

00:08:14.030 --> 00:08:16.670
It's a total mystery what goes through his mind.

00:08:17.480 --> 00:08:20.550
That's what makes him such a heartthrob!

00:08:20.550 --> 00:08:22.060
That isn't what I meant.

00:08:23.060 --> 00:08:24.970
Oh, I know that...

00:08:26.490 --> 00:08:29.940
He's a man of many faces.

00:08:30.470 --> 00:08:32.740
He has the dignified face of a leader,

00:08:33.380 --> 00:08:35.990
the affable face of a friend,

00:08:36.740 --> 00:08:39.410
and a mysterious face that bewitches people.

00:08:40.450 --> 00:08:43.890
There's no telling which one's the real him...

00:08:45.040 --> 00:08:47.880
But one thing's for sure: he isn't a fickle man.

00:08:51.600 --> 00:08:55.870
There's no need to go to Nijo Castle, Lord Hideyori!

00:08:55.870 --> 00:08:58.370
It was Lord Hideyoshi that 
ended the period of strife,

00:08:58.370 --> 00:09:02.140
but the Tokugawa clan dare look 
down on us, the Toyotomi?

00:09:02.540 --> 00:09:06.140
We can't let the Tokugawa clan 
have their way anymore!

00:09:06.140 --> 00:09:08.080
They must be taught a lesson!

00:09:08.080 --> 00:09:11.300
Now is the time for the Toyotomi 
clan to demonstrate their might!

00:09:11.780 --> 00:09:13.860
Then, basically, you're saying...

00:09:15.310 --> 00:09:16.910
You're prepared to go to war?

00:09:24.230 --> 00:09:25.330
Well?

00:09:26.920 --> 00:09:31.420
Edo

00:09:46.320 --> 00:09:48.190
The townspeople all had smiles on their faces.

00:09:48.940 --> 00:09:50.210
Oh?

00:09:50.830 --> 00:09:55.270
Is this what you'd call a world full of smiles, too?

00:09:56.760 --> 00:09:58.950
What are you getting at?

00:09:59.380 --> 00:10:01.070
I feel betrayed.

00:10:01.620 --> 00:10:04.500
All along, this was Ieyasu's plan.

00:10:04.840 --> 00:10:08.410
He wanted to pass Lord Hideyoshi's 
creation off as his own.

00:10:08.410 --> 00:10:10.460
Get to the point.

00:10:11.560 --> 00:10:13.580
And then, there's the second 
Tokugawa shogun thing.

00:10:13.580 --> 00:10:15.460
Basically, he declared to the world

00:10:15.890 --> 00:10:17.910
that the Toyotomi clan can get lost,

00:10:18.830 --> 00:10:21.180
and that Tokugawa rule will continue.

00:10:24.660 --> 00:10:28.110
Just call a spade a spade! 
The Tokugawa clan are thieves!

00:10:28.110 --> 00:10:29.910
I cannot let that slide.

00:10:31.390 --> 00:10:32.600
Takatora?

00:10:32.940 --> 00:10:35.400
Did you just call the Tokugawa clan thieves?

00:10:37.290 --> 00:10:39.060
Eavesdropping, are we?

00:10:39.060 --> 00:10:40.740
And what of it?

00:10:41.230 --> 00:10:42.760
I have to say...

00:10:42.760 --> 00:10:46.240
Your recent, obvious support for the 
Toyotomi clan is getting on my nerves.

00:10:48.000 --> 00:10:51.540
I hope you aren't planning to 
betray the Tokugawa clan.

00:10:51.540 --> 00:10:53.470
"Betray the Tokugawa clan"?

00:10:53.470 --> 00:10:56.000
We've always been the Toyotomi clan's vassals.

00:10:57.010 --> 00:10:59.510
Then you refuse to serve the Tokugawa clan?

00:11:00.210 --> 00:11:03.260
The Tokugawa clan are also supposed 
to be Toyotomi vassals!

00:11:03.700 --> 00:11:06.390
Unlike you, we don't switch allegiances 
at the drop of a hat.

00:11:08.390 --> 00:11:10.520
If it's a fight you want, bring it on!

00:11:30.350 --> 00:11:31.290
That's enough!

00:11:34.290 --> 00:11:36.540
Put away your weapons.

00:11:36.540 --> 00:11:37.850
Lord Tadakatsu...

00:11:41.300 --> 00:11:44.630
As long as this ends now, I'll keep it to myself.

00:11:45.810 --> 00:11:47.150
Understood?

00:11:47.560 --> 00:11:48.700
Yes, sir.

00:12:07.850 --> 00:12:09.890
Please wait! You mustn't!

00:12:10.870 --> 00:12:14.070
We've been ordered to not let anyone see him!

00:12:19.190 --> 00:12:21.050
Yukimura Sanada...

00:12:21.830 --> 00:12:23.710
Lord Naomasa Ii...

00:12:27.300 --> 00:12:28.320
Who?

00:12:28.320 --> 00:12:29.560
Lord Yukimura!

00:12:30.300 --> 00:12:31.390
Stay out of this.

00:12:32.190 --> 00:12:33.400
You're...

00:12:34.520 --> 00:12:35.840
Stand down.

00:12:36.640 --> 00:12:37.580
But...

00:12:50.160 --> 00:12:51.120
Yukimura,

00:12:52.170 --> 00:12:53.410
take up your spear.

00:13:06.750 --> 00:13:10.720
A fleeting time of quiet is not Lord Ieyasu's desire.

00:13:10.720 --> 00:13:12.890
It's a long-lasting world of peace.

00:13:13.560 --> 00:13:18.230
In order to realize that dream, warriors such 
as you must be done away with.

00:13:18.900 --> 00:13:22.740
That said, I respect you as a warrior.

00:13:22.740 --> 00:13:25.400
I shall let you go out in a blaze of glory.

00:13:26.260 --> 00:13:27.910
Take up your spear, Yukimura!

00:13:29.120 --> 00:13:32.410
I shall never take up arms again.

00:13:38.210 --> 00:13:40.170
So you're willing to die on your backside?

00:13:40.970 --> 00:13:43.420
I'm afraid I cannot die, either.

00:13:44.740 --> 00:13:47.590
You say you want to live, despite being disgraced?

00:13:48.000 --> 00:13:49.420
You're out of your mind.

00:13:52.380 --> 00:13:55.460
It's fine to consider living shameful.

00:13:55.880 --> 00:13:58.770
However, you should also consider 
why you were kept alive.

00:14:00.040 --> 00:14:02.230
No matter how shameful my life may be,

00:14:02.230 --> 00:14:04.860
I cannot afford to die.

00:14:04.860 --> 00:14:06.890
Because it's the promise I made to my brother.

00:14:07.820 --> 00:14:09.070
Nobuyuki?

00:14:09.070 --> 00:14:12.280
He said your execution would be 
understandable, you know.

00:14:12.490 --> 00:14:16.880
Even so, he told me to live on.

00:14:17.490 --> 00:14:21.740
To consider what it means to live... 
What it means for me to stay in this world.

00:14:22.580 --> 00:14:24.470
Until I find that answer,

00:14:24.850 --> 00:14:26.800
I cannot die.

00:14:27.250 --> 00:14:29.530
Well, I can't leave you alive!

00:14:30.960 --> 00:14:34.060
You're a threat to the Tokugawa clan's world.

00:14:34.350 --> 00:14:38.310
I'm in confinement. What could I possibly do?

00:14:38.580 --> 00:14:40.130
You're alive!

00:14:40.520 --> 00:14:42.310
That alone makes you dangerous.

00:14:45.220 --> 00:14:47.190
Take up your spear, Yukimura!

00:14:54.070 --> 00:14:57.080
I decided to never hold a spear again.

00:14:59.030 --> 00:15:01.040
So be it.

00:15:01.040 --> 00:15:02.780
Die, Yukimura!

00:15:05.060 --> 00:15:06.170
Lord Yukimura!

00:15:14.700 --> 00:15:16.180
Are you injured?

00:15:22.210 --> 00:15:23.700
The wind is carrying a strange scent...

00:15:32.860 --> 00:15:33.520
The village!

00:15:33.520 --> 00:15:34.460
What?

00:15:38.220 --> 00:15:39.230
Wh-What's going on?

00:15:39.230 --> 00:15:41.000
A fire? How?

00:15:48.480 --> 00:15:50.370
What's happening to the village?

00:15:52.590 --> 00:15:53.300
Yukimura!

00:15:58.470 --> 00:16:00.180
This way, everyone!

00:16:04.000 --> 00:16:04.940
Who goes there?

00:16:10.890 --> 00:16:12.530
Kotaro Fuma...

00:16:13.460 --> 00:16:15.750
Tsukimaru, get everyone to safety!

00:16:24.290 --> 00:16:26.290
<i>I have to protect the villagers!</i>

00:16:27.830 --> 00:16:29.340
Run away, everyone!

00:16:30.000 --> 00:16:31.010
Lord Yukimura!

00:16:31.010 --> 00:16:32.090
Hurry!

00:16:43.760 --> 00:16:45.100
Hurry up and escape!

00:17:05.550 --> 00:17:06.210
Miss!

00:17:08.090 --> 00:17:09.710
Sink into the depths of chaos.

00:17:21.020 --> 00:17:22.140
Lord Yukimura!

00:17:22.350 --> 00:17:23.640
Lord Yukimura!

00:17:24.010 --> 00:17:24.810
Yukimura!

00:17:30.990 --> 00:17:32.900
Take up your spear, Yukimura!

00:17:34.760 --> 00:17:36.650
You are a samurai warrior!

00:17:51.240 --> 00:17:52.420
Lord Yukimura!

00:17:57.430 --> 00:18:01.430
<i>I have people I must protect.</i>

00:18:01.770 --> 00:18:04.060
<i>That is the meaning of my life!</i>

00:18:31.080 --> 00:18:32.090
Lord Naomasa...

00:18:36.650 --> 00:18:38.300
Get on my back, Suzu!

00:18:54.930 --> 00:18:56.150
Lord Naomasa!

00:18:56.610 --> 00:18:57.400
Never mind me!

00:19:17.980 --> 00:19:19.200
Yukimura,

00:19:20.000 --> 00:19:24.340
fight me next...

00:19:33.100 --> 00:19:34.690
I won't fall for the same trick twice!

00:19:40.290 --> 00:19:40.950
Futile!

00:20:12.110 --> 00:20:13.540
Wake up.

00:20:17.520 --> 00:20:18.620
You...

00:20:18.620 --> 00:20:20.770
War is upon us.

00:20:20.770 --> 00:20:22.480
What are you talking about?

00:20:42.930 --> 00:20:44.480
Lord Naomasa...

00:21:00.040 --> 00:21:03.750
All my life, I've been fighting to protect something.

00:21:04.780 --> 00:21:06.950
In Ueda, it was my people.

00:21:07.340 --> 00:21:09.490
This time, it was the village.

00:21:10.220 --> 00:21:13.370
Therefore, I cannot stay here anymore.

00:21:13.870 --> 00:21:16.360
Then, in order to protect it, you'll leave?

00:21:16.690 --> 00:21:19.960
This village is precious to me, so I must.

00:21:20.510 --> 00:21:24.480
For I cannot live as anything but a warrior.

00:21:27.930 --> 00:21:29.290
Lord Yukimura...

00:21:41.020 --> 00:21:44.320
As you are now, I want you to hold on to it.

00:21:50.090 --> 00:21:51.550
Lord Mitsunari...

00:21:56.010 --> 00:22:01.150
I shall never forget the vow of 
righteousness I shared with you!

00:23:41.890 --> 00:23:45.150
Sengoku Musou 
High School

00:23:41.890 --> 00:23:45.150
7th Period

00:23:45.580 --> 00:23:47.150
Here's your order!

00:23:47.480 --> 00:23:49.170
And here's your change.

00:23:49.170 --> 00:23:50.900
It's one million yen!

00:23:55.010 --> 00:23:57.350
A smile's zero yen!

00:24:00.510 --> 00:24:01.660
Here you go.

00:24:01.660 --> 00:24:03.690
Is that even edible?!

00:24:05.250 --> 00:24:08.880
Ninja Burgers

00:24:07.810 --> 00:24:08.880
Chaos.

00:24:08.880 --> 00:24:09.880
<i>To Be Continued</i>

00:24:09.880 --> 00:24:24.800
<i>Next Episode</i>

00:24:10.750 --> 00:24:14.930
The next departure is for the bridge that 
leads to the place where one belongs.

00:24:14.930 --> 00:24:16.880
They won't come to a standstill anymore.

00:24:17.080 --> 00:24:20.850
They'll only believe in themselves, 
pressing ever onward.

00:24:21.100 --> 00:24:23.850
Next time: "The Path of No Return."

00:24:22.020 --> 00:24:24.800
<i>Episode Eight 
The Path of No Return</i>
